WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.310
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:03.700
[APPLAUSE]

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:04.670
Good evening.

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:06.940
And here are the nominees
for Best Original Song.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.920
We really did not expect to win.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:10.930
It was like finding--

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:13.060
I mean, just being
nominated was like finding

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.470
$20 in your pocket.

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:16.780
It was very nice
and very surprising

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.010
when they called our name.

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:20.260
When Lin said, México.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:24.450
México, Kristen Anderson-Lopez
and Robert Lopez for Remember

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:24.950
Me.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.710
[APPLAUSE]

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:29.260
The first thing I thought
is I got to hug the kids.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.960
I'm so glad they're
here to see that.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.450
It was really special
to have them there

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:36.430
and to be able to
shout out to them.

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:39.040
And our daughters, Katie and
Annie, who are here with us

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.960
tonight.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:46.120
Your love and creativity
inspire everything we do.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.670
We wrote Remember
Me because we're

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:51.190
songwriters who have to
leave our kids behind,

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.620
and we leave them little
songs that they can sing.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:56.140
(SINGING) So I sing
a secret song to you

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.710
each night we are apart.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:02.605
(SINGING) I sing a secret song
to you each night we are apart.

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:08.480
Remember Me.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.800
We left them with lullabies so
they could feel our presence.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:16.100
And so, I think there wouldn't
be the same Remember Me

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:17.810
without those two girls.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.970
It's crazy, that song--

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:21.200
writing Remember Me.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.170
Very shortly after we wrote
it, my grandmother passed away,

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:28.340
and then sadly, a few
years later, my mom

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:29.660
lost a battle with cancer.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:37.310
And that song helped me realize
that it's through our memories

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:39.200
that our loved ones live on.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:42.080
And there's feeling
of a family reunion

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:46.070
to Coco, a family reunion that
can cross the life and death

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:46.670
barrier.

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.512
That is a really, really
beautiful thought,

00:01:48.512 --> 00:01:50.720
and I think that's why people
love the movie so much.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:52.730
This is for my mom
who passed away.

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:55.970
Everyone who knew her
will always remember her.

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:57.170
[APPLAUSE]

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.620
[MUSIC PLAYING]

